The fastest-moving progressed planet is the Moon, moving at 
a rate of approximately 12? per year. There are two features of 
the progressed Moon which are non-chart-related, one is the 
change of zodiac sign, which occurs approximately every two- 
and-a-half years; and the other is the angular relationship to 
the progressed Sun-the Progressed Lunar phase. 


