house. 

This Aries New Moon in the 9th house wonderfully de- 
scribes a man who is remembered for pioneering work and 
ideas (Aries) and who had published in the academic world 
(9th house). Indeed, in 1589 Galileo published his first treatise 
on the center of gravity in solid objects. Here we see the 12? 
orb coming into effect. 

